  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the highest-priority question is establishing a performance floor. config_007 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000, no aggregation, no fusion) is the simplest possible configuration: it requires no trained encoder (PCA is instantaneous), uses a single profile, and has no aggregation or fusion steps. This gives us a clean, fast, low-risk baseline that will serve as the reference point for every subsequent comparison—whether multiprofile helps, whether image modality adds value, whether learned encoders (scgpt, scvi) outperform PCA, and whether aggregation/fusion strategies improve performance. Starting here minimizes implementation risk, is computationally cheap, and maximizes the interpretability of all future deltas. Without this floor, we cannot determine whether any added complexity actually contributes."
}

